olute after:inset-0\",\"children\":\"The Freelance Payment Penalty: A Modeled Audit of Platform Fees, FX Spreads, and Payout Delays\"}]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-slate-600 text-sm mb-6 flex-grow line-clamp-3 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"The money rarely disappears through a single, easy-to-spot fee. The real loss is stacked. A marketplace takes its commission, a processor adds a charge for international cards, a bank or payment company converts the currency at a spread, a platform holds the funds before release, and a wire sheds a little to intermediaries on the way in. Each layer looks defensible on its own, but the worker feels the combined result as a smaller deposit and a later payday.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center justify-between pt-4 border-t border-slate-50 mt-auto\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-wrap gap-1\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",\"freelance payment fees\",{\"className\":\"text-xs bg-slate-100 text-slate-700 px-2 py-1 rounded-full hover:bg-slate-200 transition-colors\",\"children\":\"freelance payment fees\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"cross-border payments\",{\"className\":\"text-xs bg-slate-100 text-slate-700 px-2 py-1 rounded-full hover:bg-slate-200 transition-colors\",\"children\":\"cross-border payments\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"platform fees\",{\"className\":\"text-xs bg-slate-100 text-slate-700 px-2 py-1 rounded-full hover:bg-slate-200 transition-colors\",\"children\":\"platform fees\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-brand-primary text-sm font-bold transition-colors flex items-center\",\"children\":[\"Read\",[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"ml-1 h-3.5 w-3.5 transform transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-1\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"d\":\"M14 5l7 7m0 0l-7 7m7-7H3\"}]}]]}]]}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",\"how-to-respond-to-a-subpoena-for-business-records\",{\"className\":\"relative group bg-white rounded-2xl transition-all duration-300 overflow-hidden border border-slate-200 hover:border-slate-300 hover:shadow-lg hover:-translate-y-1 flex flex-col h-full\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"h-40 w-full overflow-hidden relative \",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L2d\",null,{\"src\":\"https://images.pexels.com/photos/6170642/pexels-photo-6170642.jpeg?auto=compress\u0026cs=tinysrgb\u0026w=600\u0026q=80\",\"alt\":\"How to Respond to a Subpoena for Business Records\",\"fill\":true,\"className\":\"object-cover\",\"sizes\":\"(min-width: 1024px) 25vw, (min-width: 768px) 33vw, 100vw\"}]}],\"$Lf3\"]}],\"$Lf4\"]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"e8:[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"pr-6 font-medium\",\"children\":\"Which compliance artifacts do acquirers expect first?\"}]\ne9:[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"w-5 h-5 text-slate-400 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"d\":\"M19 9l-7 7-7-7\"}]}]\nea:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base text-slate-600 leading-relaxed px-5 pb-5 border-t border-slate-100 pt-4 prose prose-headings:text-slate-900 prose-p:text-slate-600 prose-strong:text-slate-900 prose-li:text-slate-600 max-w-none\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-0\",{\"children\":\"Start with records showing the compliance program is operating, not just documented. Useful first artifacts include current monitoring output, issue logs, corrective-action records, training records, and named control ownership. Buyers want evidence the program can stay effective through disruption.\"}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"eb:[\"$\",\"details\",\"3\",{\"data-faq\":true,\"open\":false,\"className\":\"group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white overflow-hidden\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"cursor-pointer list-none text-lg text-slate-900 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-brand-teal focus-visible:ring-inset flex items-center justify-between px-5 py-5 hover:bg-slate-50/80 group-hover:text-brand-teal transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"pr-6 font-medium\",\"children\":\"How do technical controls change valuation and integration risk?\"}],[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"w-5 h-5 text-slate-400 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"d\":\"M19 9l-7 7-7-7\"}]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base text-slate-600 leading-relaxed px-5 pb-5 border-t border-slate-100 pt-4 prose prose-headings:text-slate-900 prose-p:text-slate-600 prose-strong:text-slate-900 prose-li:text-slate-600 max-w-none\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-0\",{\"children\":\"They affect buyer confidence because they shape expected integration effort. Heavy technical debt, incompatibility with existing systems, and non-compliance issues are known due-diligence alarm bells. Unresolved technical debt can raise execution risk and increase post-close remediation work.\"}]]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"ec:[\"$\",\"details\",\"4\",{\"data-faq\":true,\"open\":false,\"className\":\"group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white overflow-hidden\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"cursor-pointer list-none text-lg text-slate-900 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-brand-teal focus-visible:ring-inset flex items-center justify-between px-5 py-5 hover:bg-slate-50/80 group-hover:text-brand-teal transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"pr-6 font-medium\",\"children\":\"How should founders prioritize country expansion against compliance complexity?\"}],[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"w-5 h-5 text-slate-400 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"d\":\"M19 9l-7 7-7-7\"}]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base text-slate-600 leading-relaxed px-5 pb-5 border-t border-slate-100 pt-4 prose prose-headings:text-slate-900 prose-p:text-slate-600 prose-strong:text-slate-900 prose-li:text-slate-600 max-w-none\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-0\",{\"children\":\"Use a risk-based approach instead of giving every market equal effort. Apply deeper review to higher-risk relationships and lighter review to lower-risk services. Prioritize markets where your operating model and controls are already demonstrable, and hold conditional markets until the evidence is solid.\"}]]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"ed:[\"$\",\"details\",\"5\",{\"data-faq\":true,\"open\":false,\"className\":\"group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white overflow-hidden\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"cursor-pointer list-none text-lg text-slate-900 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-brand-teal focus-visible:ring-inset flex items-center justify-between px-5 py-5 hover:bg-slate-50/80 group-hover:text-brand-teal transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"pr-6 font-medium\",\"children\":\"What are the most common Day 1 post-merger failure points?\"}],[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"w-5 h-5 text-slate-400 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"d\":\"M19 9l-7 7-7-7\"}]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base text-slate-600 leading-relaxed px-5 pb-5 border-t border-slate-100 pt-4 prose prose-headings:text-slate-900 prose-p:text-slate-600 prose-strong:text-slate-900 prose-li:text-slate-600 max-w-none\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-0\",{\"children\":\"The most common Day 1 failures are operational: payroll, systems, customer support, controls, approvals, or leadership decisions are not ready to function together at closing. Another recurring risk is post-acquisition vendor disruption, including product sunsets and support degradation from personnel loss. These failures are especially damaging because the compliance program is still expected to remain effective through disruption.\"}]]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"ee:[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"\\n            (function(){\\n              try {\\n                const script = document.currentScript;\\n                const section = script \u0026\u0026 script.closest('[data-faq-section]');\\n                if (!section) return;\\n                const btn = section.querySelector('[data-faq-toggle]');\\n                if (!btn) return;\\n                btn.addEventListener('click', function(){\\n                  const items = Array.from(section.querySelectorAll('[data-faq]'));\\n                  if (!items.length) return;\\n                  const allOpen = items.every(i =\u003e i.open);\\n                  items.forEach(i =\u003e i.open = !allOpen);\\n                  btn.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(!allOpen));\\n                  btn.textContent = allOpen ? 'Expand all' : 'Collapse all';\\n                });\\n              } catch (e) { console.warn(e); }\\n            })();\\n          \"}}]\nf5:Tafa,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What does acquisition-ready mean for a payment platform in practical terms?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"It means Day 1 readiness: the buyer, target, or combined company can function legally and operationally at closing. Core operations and controls need to work in production, not just in presentations. If controls, approvals, or customer support break at close, readiness was overstated.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What must be ready before buyer diligence starts?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Before diligence starts, have a clear, current operating evidence set that can be reviewed quickly and updated as diligence progresses. The process is systematic and typically runs through stages rather than a single upload. Be ready for periodic reassessment and risk-profile updates.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Which compliance artifacts do acquirers expect first?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Start with records showing the compliance program is operating, not just documented. Useful first artifacts include current monitoring output, issue logs, corrective-action records, training records, and named control ownership. Buyers want evidence the program can stay effective through disruption.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How do technical controls change valuation and integration risk?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"They affect buyer confidence because they shape expected integration effort. Heavy technical debt, incompatibility with existing systems, and non-compliance issues are known due-diligence alarm bells. Unresolved technical debt can raise execution risk and increase post-close remediation work.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How should founders prioritize country expansion against compliance complexity?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Use a risk-based approach instead of giving every market equal effort. Apply deeper review to higher-risk relationships and lighter review to lower-risk services. Prioritize markets where your operating model and controls are already demonstrable, and hold conditional markets until the evidence is solid.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What are the most common Day 1 post-merger failure points?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"The most common Day 1 failures are operational: payroll, systems, customer support, controls, approvals, or leadership decisions are not ready to function together at closing. Another recurring risk is post-acquisition vendor disruption, including product sunsets and support degradation from personnel loss. These failures are especially damaging because the compliance program is still expected to remain effective through disruption.\"}}]}"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"ef:[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$f5\"}}]\nf0:[\"$\",\"li\",\"https://dodcio.defense.gov/Portals/0/Documents/Library/RequirementsAcquisitionDigitalCapabilitiesGuidebook.pdf\",{\"data-source-trust\":\"trusted\",\"className\":\"leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://dodcio.defense.gov/Portals/0/Documents/Library/RequirementsAcquisitionDigitalCapabilitiesGuidebook.pdf\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"className\":\"text-teal-700 hover:text-teal-800 hover:underline\",\"title\":\"https://dodcio.defense.gov/Portals/0/Documents/Library/RequirementsAcquisitionDigitalCapabilitiesGuidebook.pdf\",\"children\":\"dodcio.defense.gov/Portals/0/Documents/Library/RequirementsAcqu...\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"ml-2 inline-block rounded-xl px-2 py-0.5 text-eyebrow-sm uppercase tracking-wide bg-teal-50 text-teal-700\",\"children\":\"trusted\"}]]}]\nf1:[\"$\",\"li\",\"http